This resolution was adopted by the Board of Directors of SPI at their
"face to face" meeting on November 19th, 2026.

# Resolution 2026-11-19.mcs.1: Appointment of Secretary Pro Tempore **DRAFT**

WHEREAS, Katherine (Katie) McMillan currently serves as the appointed
Secretary of Software in the Public Interest, Inc. ("SPI");

WHEREAS, the current availability status of *Katie McMillan*
is unknown, creating an immediate operational need to ensure continuity in
corporate governance, record-keeping, and secretarial duties; and

WHEREAS, the Board of Directors deems it necessary and in the best interest
of SPI to appoint an interim officer to fulfill the responsibilities of the
Secretary until such time as Katie McMillan's availability status is
clarified and resolved;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED THAT:

   1. Jeremy Stanley is hereby appointed to serve as Secretary Pro Tempore
   of Software in the Public Interest, Inc., effective immediately upon the
   adoption of this resolution.

   2. In this capacity, Jeremy Stanley is authorized and directed to
   perform all duties and exercise all powers incident to the office of the
   Secretary as set forth in the SPI Bylaws and corporate policies, including
   but not limited to recording meeting minutes, maintaining corporate
   records, and managing official correspondence.

   3. This interim appointment shall remain in full force and effect until
   such time as the Board of Directors determines that the availability status
   of Secretary Katie McMillan has been adequately resolved, or until a
   successor is duly appointed or elected by the Board.
